 "question": "Compare supervised and unsupervised learning.",
 "answer": "Supervised learning involves training examples with labels, where the model learns a mapping from features X to a target y, applicable in tasks like classification (e.g., spam detection) and regression (e.g., predicting house prices) [S1] [S4]. Unsupervised learning, on the other hand, lacks labels, aiming to discover structure in data, such as clustering similar examples or reducing dimensions [S1] [S4].",
